Package: ordinalDualresponse
Title: Ordinal Dual-Response Choice Models for Conjoint Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Dan", "Yavorsky", email = "dyavorsky@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Prachi", "Bhalerao", role = "ctb"),
    person("Geoffery", "Zheng", role = "ctb"))
Description: Simulation, estimation, and design tools for choice-based conjoint
    studies with an ordinal dual-response follow-up question ("how likely are
    you to buy the option you selected?"). Implements the joint likelihood of
    a forced multinomial-logit choice and a cumulative-link ordinal purchase
    evaluation driven by the task's inclusive value, under a Gumbel link
    (probability-report behavioral model) or a logistic link (graded-comparison
    model). The two-point scale collapses exactly to the binary dual-response
    models of Diener, Orme and Yardley (2006) and Hung et al. (2025). Includes
    maximum-likelihood and hierarchical Bayesian (random-walk Metropolis within
    Gibbs) estimators, heterogeneous cut points, Fisher-information and
    scale-design tools, specification tests for the unit inclusive-value slope
    and for DR-2Max conditioning, model-comparison utilities (Newton-Raftery,
    bridge sampling, WAIC, holdout likelihood), and Nash-pricing counterfactual
    helpers.
